# The application bundle is byte-exact and identified by its sha256. Git must
# not rewrite its line endings: the file ships with CRLF, normalisation would
# not change how it runs but would invalidate the hash, and the hash is how a
# bug report is matched to the build it came from.
#
# Re-verify after any tooling change:  sha256sum index.html
# The expected value lives in README.md rather than here, because it changes
# with every release and a hash pinned in two places goes stale in one of them.

/index.html -text

*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
404.html text eol=lf
